     I was playing a priest (still am, actually) today, and god lucky
with the altars.  My God was handing me more artifacts than I could
deal with (all the neutral ones, as a matter of fact; all four of them
in about five sacrifices).  After upgrading from Frost Brand to Fire
Brand (is that an upgrade?  Not sure myself), I found I had enough money
(no pickaxe yet) to buy that bag of holding in the shop.  Soooo... I
stowed away all my extra weapons, and went on with my business.  The
tool shop also had a magic lamp (did you know you can pretty much identify
magic lamps when you find a bunch of lamps lying around?), blessed it
and got ahold of +3 gray scale (an AC of -8 and Fire Brand makes a damn
good priest, if you ask me) for the first time (always came up +0 with
my other games, even with a luck of 10).  I could have gone for speed
boots, but they can wait.  I've had priests fall to soldier ants with
speed boots, but the gray scale improves my AC enough to get over that
obstacle.  Got blinded by a yellow light (hate it when they show up
before I get telepathy), walked over whatever it was that killed an
archeologist on dlvl 5 (now I have a pickaxe, albeit I'm down to 1
potion of holy water, since the magic lamp started out cursed).
     Now, the bug.  I was taking things out of the bag, and I got
prompted with: "a wide sword".  A wide sword?  Did I forget and
stow some junk in there?  No, wait, that was Giantslayer.  What's going
on?  I backtracked, pulled the weapons out of the bag (all three of
'em, no names) and they were still nameless.  I'm stuck with two long
swords (I suppose I can get Excalibur, but Fire Brand works much
better unless you're faced with a horde of undead) and a broadsword
now, instead of Dragonbane, Giantslayer, and Frost Brand.  Sheesh!
     So... does the game still think those three weapons exist, even
though my bag of holding (I'm playing a priest-- of course it wasn't
cursed) seems to have appropriated their identities?
     I'll send this to nethack-bugs@linc.cis.upenn.edu as well, in more
abbreviated form.
     It's not so bad.  I should still be able to make it to the castle
with this guy, and at least I won't have to worry about other monsters
getting ahold of special weapons (that's why I put them in the bag rather
than under a boulder, really, although it'd be nice to be able to pull
out Dragonbane every so often, and perhaps Frost Brand if I were losing
a fight against a fire elemental and had intrinsic fire resistance).
     Last time I put named weapons in a bag, however.  I certainly hope
chests are safe, though, since giants can walk over boulders and dwarves
can tunnel through walls, and both can wield what they pick up.


